WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:06.759
People are calling dishonor on Disney's live-action
Mulan after the star of the upcoming remake,

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:10.860
Crystal Liu, posted on social media in support
of the Hong Kong police force.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.170
Liu's admission of support of Hong Kong law
enforcement, which has been under scrutiny

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:20.240
for what human rights groups have deemed an
excessive use of force against pro-democracy

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.420
protesters, sparked outrage in China and caused
a ripple effect around the world.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.740
Taking to Weibo, the Chinese social media
site on which Liu has over 65 million followers,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.869
the actress shared an image that reads,

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:37.290
"I support Hong Kong's police, you can all
attack me now...What a shame for Hong Kong."

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:43.059
She hashtagged the image, originally shared
by the Chinese newspaper group People's Daily,

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:46.420
#IAlsoSupportTheHongKongPolice, then added
a heart emoji.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:51.940
Less than 24 hours after Liu posted the photo,
it amassed over 72,000 likes and was shared

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.160
over 65,000 times.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.379
Backlash has been just as swift, though.

00:00:56.379 --> 00:01:01.819
The hashtag #BoycottMulan has taken over Twitter
and Instagram in the time since Liu's post,

00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:05.159
with the tag feed filling up with dozens of
posts per hour.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:06.829
One user on Twitter wrote,

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:11.180
"Support Liu's Mulan = Support Police's Abuse
of Power.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:16.440
The spirit of Mulan is about bravery, not
fighting the citizens with unlimited force."

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.869
Another user went viral with his #BoycottMulan
tweet that reads,

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:27.210
"Disney's Mulan actress, Liu Yifei, supports
police brutality and oppression in Hong Kong.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.689
Liu is a naturalized American citizen.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.110
it must be nice.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.690
meanwhile she p---es on people fighting for
democracy.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:34.800
retweet please.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.689
HK doesn't get enough support.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:39.710
#BoycottMulan @Disney."

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:40.710
Another added,

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.440
"I thought people were just overreacting at
first but yikes.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:48.030
She really just f---ed over that movie and
all involved.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.450
The movie's budget was already rumored to
be pretty large too.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.369
A simple recast won't fix this issue.

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:58.350
They'd have to likely reshoot the entire film.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.680
#BoycottMulan."

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.610
Over on Instagram, user @rileyscreed shared
a post that read in part,

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:08.600
"...if you support what the police are doing
in Hong Kong, you are unbelievably ignorant.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.840
They violate human rights for fun.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.010
She comes from such a place of entitlement
it's not surprising that her closed mind would

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.120
spew out this trash."

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.290
So what's this all about?

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.810
In recent months, the Hong Kong police force
has been the center of an intense debate about

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.830
police brutality, democracy, and the autonomy
of Hong Kong.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.000
In June, hundreds of thousands of people in
Hong Kong gathered to protest a bill that

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.980
would grant criminally charged residents the
possibility to be extradited from the Hong

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.110
Kong city-state to mainland China.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:43.531
Protesters fought against the bill, arguing
that it would destroy Hong Kong's autonomy

00:02:43.531 --> 00:02:48.850
that it established under the "one country,
two systems" standard in 1997.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:53.830
Local police have since implemented increasingly
aggressive tactics to dissuade protesters

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:59.090
and clear the streets, going so far as to
use tear gas in enclosed spaces and shoot

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.680
rubber bullets into crowds, seriously injuring
and even blinding protesters.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.730
As things have escalated, activists' focus
has evolved from the proposed bill in particular

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.570
to general outrage over police brutality and
a fight for democracy in Hong Kong.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:18.100
On top of that, Variety reported that Facebook
and Twitter have been forced to crackdown

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.290
on what is believed to be an attempt by the
Chinese government to intentionally spread

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:26.180
misinformation about the protests on social
media - using Mulan.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:32.310
And while social media bots spread pro-government
Mulan memes, the official state-backed media

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.960
have begun hyping the film as well.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.840
Complicating things even further, there's
the fact that Chinese stars are sometimes

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:43.370
forced to publicly support government policies
regardless of their personal feelings.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:48.820
In 2018, the nation's biggest movie star,
Fan Bingbing, completely vanished without

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.820
a trace for six months.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.930
It was later learned that she had been placed
under house arrest for failure to pay taxes

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.210
on her movie earnings.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:00.650
Upon her release, Bingbing issued a repentant
propaganda statement praising the Chinese

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:06.260
government, which raises the question of whether
Mulan star Liu posted the pro-government comments

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.870
of her own free will to begin with.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:13.850
"Celebrities like Jackie Chan and film studios
are required by the government to support

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.830
core sociaist values."

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.980
All of which puts Disney in a very tricky
spot which would seem to make it difficult

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:24.830
for the company to recast the role, especially
since the movie has already been filmed.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.710
There is some precedent, though.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:32.210
In 2017, just weeks before the release of
the crime thriller All the Money in the World,

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:36.070
star Kevin Spacey was accused of numerous
instances of sexual assault.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:41.410
Director Ridley Scott decided to remove Spacey
from the film entirely, and reshot all of

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.450
his scenes with Christopher Plummer in the
role instead.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.840
In any case, a boycott of this caliber isn't
good for any party connected to Mulan.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.710
Liu's statement doesn't bode well for her
public image, it doesn't help the people of

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:58.320
Hong Kong exposed to the chaos currently overtaking
the city-state, and it casts shadows on Disney,

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.040
which goes to great lengths to maintain a
squeaky-clean reputation.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.820
Only time will tell whether the boycott will
impact the film, which is currently scheduled

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.900
to open in theaters on March 27, 2020.

